let __v_593 = Value::from("A birth weight between about 5lb 8oz and 8lb 13oz is normal, and the number on its own says very little: what matters is the line in the red book. A baby usually gets back to their birth weight by two weeks and then gains roughly 150 to 200g a week for the first few months, so the health visitor plotting it once is worth more than any single figure. Ask them to weigh the baby if you are unsure, and go sooner if the gain flattens off, if there are fewer than six wet nappies a day, or if the baby is too sleepy to feed.");
